{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityBWedderburn","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityBWedderburn","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Pi","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.Finite.Matrix","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Equiv.Fin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Option","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.MatrixAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Central.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.WedderburnArtin","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.IsAlgClosed","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Maschke","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityBCentrality"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:identityB_via_wedderburn_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"identityB_via_wedderburn_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L311-L322","doc":"**Identity (B) for `ℂ[S_n]`, fully sorry-free.** Same conclusion as\n`identityB_via_wedderburn`, with the centrality `C₂ ∈ Set.center ℂ[Sₙ]` discharged by\n`IdentityBCentrality.centralC2_mem_center` (Jucys' theorem, machine-checked: the coefficient of\n`C₂` is a class function — `binom(n,2)` at `1`, `1` at each 3-cycle, `0` elsewhere). Every link —\nthe Wedderburn block decomposition, the quadratic dimension weighting, `∑ dᵢ² = n!`, side-1\n`trace = n!·binom`, the center-reduction machinery, and the 3-cycle count — is proved; axioms:\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:identityB_via_wedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"identityB_via_wedderburn","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L287-L309","doc":"**Identity (B) for `ℂ[S_n]`, conditional only on the centrality of `C₂`.** There exist block\ndimensions `d : Fin N → ℕ` and block scalars `ω : Fin N → ℂ` with\n`∑ dᵢ² = n!` (Artin–Wedderburn sum-of-squares) and `∑ dᵢ²·ωᵢ = n!·binom(n,2)` (**Identity (B)**),\nthe only hypothesis being that the Jucys–Murphy central element `C₂ = ∑_k X_k²` is central. The\nquadratic weighting and `∑ dᵢ² = n!` are derived, not assumed; reading `ωᵢ = ∑_{c∈λᵢ} c(c)²` and\n`dᵢ = #SYT(λᵢ)` (the two OV labelling bricks, out of scope) makes this the literal Plancherel\ncontent-square mean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.trace_mulLeft_central_eq_block_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.trace_mulLeft_central_eq_block_sum","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L221-L269","doc":"**Abstract trace identity, semisimple-algebra form (the abstract discharge).**\nLet `A` be a finite-dimensional algebra over an algebraically closed field `F`, with `A` semisimple\n(e.g. `A = F[G]` for a finite group with `|G|` invertible, by Maschke). For any **central** `z ∈ A`,\nthere is a finite family of block dimensions `d : Fin n → ℕ` and block scalars `ω : Fin n → F` with\n* `∑ᵢ dᵢ² = finrank_F A`  (the Artin–Wedderburn sum-of-squares), and\n* `trace_F(mulLeft z) = ∑ᵢ dᵢ²·ωᵢ`  (**Identity-(B) trace, side 2**, abstractly),\n\nobtained from the Artin–Wedderburn isomorphism `A ≃ₐ[F] ∏ᵢ Mat_{dᵢ}(F)` (Mathlib's\n`exists_algEquiv_pi_matrix_of_isAlgClosed`) by transporting `mulLeft z` (concrete Schur: `z`\ncentral ⇒ each block component is a scalar matrix `Matrix.scalar (ωᵢ)`) and applying the Pi-trace\ndecomposition. **This needs no S_n-specific Okounkov–Vershik data** — it is the generic semisimple\ntrace identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.mulLeft_algEquiv_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.mulLeft_algEquiv_conj","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L215-L219","doc":"`mulLeft` transported across an algebra equivalence is conjugation of `mulLeft`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.trace_mulLeft_pi_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.trace_mulLeft_pi_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L196-L211","doc":"**Abstract trace identity (product-of-matrices form).** For a central element `z` of\n`∏ᵢ Mat_{dᵢ}(F)` over a field `F`, the trace of left-multiplication by `z` on the regular\nrepresentation is `∑ᵢ dᵢ²·ωᵢ`, where `z i = Matrix.scalar (ω i)` is the scalar by which `z` acts on\nblock `i` (its centrality forces each component to be a scalar matrix — concrete Schur's lemma).\n\nPure linear algebra: `mulLeft z` is block-diagonal (`mulLeft_pi_eq_piMapEndo`); its trace splits as\nthe block sum (`trace_piMapEndo`); each block trace is `dᵢ²·ωᵢ` (`trace_mulLeft_scalar`). No\nrepresentation theory, no Wedderburn — this is the trace bookkeeping that the abstract decomposition\nfeeds into. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.center_pi_componentwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.center_pi_componentwise","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L185-L192","doc":"A central element of a finite product ring is central componentwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.mulLeft_pi_eq_piMapEndo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.mulLeft_pi_eq_piMapEndo","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L178-L183","doc":"Left-multiplication by an element of a finite product ring is the block-diagonal endo of the\ncomponentwise left-multiplications. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.trace_mulLeft_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.trace_mulLeft_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L165-L176","doc":"Trace of left-multiplication by the scalar matrix `c•1` on `Mat_d(F)` (a `d²`-dim free module)\nis `d²·c`. Proof: `mulLeft (c•1) = c • id`, `trace (c • id) = c · finrank = c·d²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.trace_piMapEndo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.trace_piMapEndo","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L152-L160","doc":"**Pi-trace decomposition.** The trace of the block-diagonal endomorphism\n`(x i) ↦ (f i (x i))` of `∀ i, M i` (finite-dimensional free `R`-modules) is the sum of\nblock traces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.piMapEndo_congrLeft_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.piMapEndo_congrLeft_conj","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L108-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.piMapEndo_option_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.piMapEndo_option_conj","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L102-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.piMapEndo_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.piMapEndo_apply","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L85-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AbsTrace.piMapEndo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AbsTrace.piMapEndo","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityBWedderburn.lean#L81-L83","signatureChunk":0}]}